6659540631, "full_output_budget": false}}]}, "long": {"tier": "development", "anchor": {"text": "BOLT-7319-CEDAR", "elapsed_s": 12.448332391970325, "ttft_s": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 11, "prompt_tokens": 8238, "total_tokens": 8249, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 8238, "prompt_ms": 11721.479, "prompt_per_token_ms": 1.4228549405195434, "prompt_per_second": 702.8123328122672, "predicted_n": 11, "predicted_ms": 262.37, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.237000000000002, "predicted_per_second": 38.114113656286925}, "finish_reason": "stop", "decode_tps_client": null, "end_to_end_output_tps": 0.8836524968674071, "full_output_budget": false}, "warmup": {"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system requires a shift in mindset from simply \"copying files\" to implementing a **data resilience strategy**. The goal is not just to have a copy of your data, but to ensure that you can recover that data quickly and completely regardless of the failure scenario (hardware crash, ransomware, or natural disaster).\n\nHere is a comprehensive guide to designing a reliable file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Foundation: The 3-2-1 Backup Rule\nBefore diving into technical details, adhere to the industry gold standard: the **3-2-1 Rule**.\n*   **3", "elapsed_s": 13.042056003992911, "ttft_s": 9.722794065950438, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 8269, "total_tokens": 8397, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 8269, "prompt_ms": 9310.325, "prompt_per_token_ms": 1.1259311887773613, "prompt_per_second": 888.1537432903791, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3319.053, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.13427559055118, "predicted_per_second": 38.26392648746495}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 38.26151788276702, "end_to_end_output_tps": 9.81440349288578, "full_output_budget": true}, "measured": [{"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system requires a shift in mindset from simply \"copying files\" to implementing a **data resilience strategy**. The goal is not just to have a copy of your data, but to ensure that you can recover that data quickly and completely regardless of the failure scenario (hardware crash, ransomware, or natural disaster).\n\nHere is a comprehensive guide to designing a reliable file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Strategy: The 3-2-1 Rule\nBefore diving into technical details, adhere to the industry-standard **3-2-1 Backup Rule**:\n*   **3** copies", "elapsed_s": 12.705387552035972, "ttft_s": 9.386822273023427, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 8270, "total_tokens": 8398, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 8270, "prompt_ms": 9270.386, "prompt_per_token_ms": 1.1209656590084645, "prompt_per_second": 892.0879885691922, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3318.368, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.12888188976378, "predicted_per_second": 38.271825186356665}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 38.2695500381386, "end_to_end_output_tps": 10.074466400632437, "full_output_budget": true}, {"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system requires a shift in mindset from simply \"copying files\" to implementing a **data resilience strategy**. The goal is to ensure that no matter what happens\u2014hardware failure, ransomware, or natural disaster\u2014your data can be recovered with minimal loss and downtime.\n\nHere is a comprehensive guide to designing a reliable file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Foundation: The 3-2-1 Backup Rule\nBefore choosing tools, adhere to the industry gold standard for data protection:\n*   **3 Copies of Data:** Your original data plus two backups.\n*   **", "elapsed_s": 12.675775286974385, "ttft_s": 9.353928519994952, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 8270, "total_tokens": 8398, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n